{"ver": "0.1", "info": {"id": "flsGz7", "date": "1621931252", "viewed": 107, "name": "Sliding sine rainbow", "username": "sodazot", "description": "Playing around to try to fully understand how the image is constructed overall. Mostly just a modification of the default set up when starting a new shader on here.", "likes": 6, "published": 1, "flags": 0, "usePreview": 0, "tags": ["2d", "gradient"], "hasliked": 0, "parentid": "fllGz7", "parentname": "Sliding rainbow"}, "renderpass": [{"inputs": [], "outputs": [{"id": "4dfGRr", "channel": 0}], "code": "#define pi 3.141592653589793238462643383279\nfloat speed = -100.0;\nfloat speed2 = 5.5;\nfloat scale = 1.0;\nfloat scale2 = 0.008;\n\nvoid mainImage(out vec4 fragColor, in vec2 fragCoord)\n{\n    \n    vec3 color = 0.5 + 0.5 * sin(fragCoord.y*scale2 + sin((fragCoord.x*scale + iTime*speed + vec3(0.0, iResolution.x / 3.0, iResolution / 2.0)) * (pi / (iResolution.x / 2.0))));\n\n    fragColor = vec4(color, 1.0);\n\n}\n", "name": "Image", "description": "", "type": "image"}]}